# Reverse proxy + automatic HTTPS for a hosted ni-assembly-mcp.
#
# Pairs with the README section "Deploying to Oracle Cloud (Always Free)", but
# works on any host where the container publishes port 8000 and Caddy runs on
# the host (the same shape as a generic VPS path).
#
# Caddy -- not the app -- now faces the internet, so the container MUST run with
#   NI_ASSEMBLY_MCP_HTTP_TRUST_PROXY_HEADERS=true
# or per-IP rate limiting collapses into a single shared bucket keyed on Caddy's
# address. See the WARNING at the top of the README's "Hosting over HTTP"
# section. Caddy sets X-Forwarded-For / X-Forwarded-Proto on every proxied
# request by default.
#
# Setup:
#   1. Point the domain's A (and AAAA) record at the VM's public IP.
#   2. Open inbound TCP 80 + 443 in BOTH the Oracle security list and the VM's
#      own iptables (Oracle's Ubuntu images filter by default).
#   3. Replace the two placeholders below, install at /etc/caddy/Caddyfile,
#      then: sudo systemctl reload caddy
#
# Streamable-HTTP MCP responses are long-lived text/event-stream streams; Caddy
# detects that Content-Type and disables response buffering automatically, so no
# extra flush_interval config is needed.

{
	# Let's Encrypt account email (certificate-expiry notices).
	email you@example.com
}

mcp.example.com {
	encode zstd gzip
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8000
}
